<title>NETHERLANDS: Fokker unit wins Indonesia test-kit order.</title>
<headline>Fokker unit wins Indonesia test-kit order.</headline>
<dateline>LEIDEN, Netherlands 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fokker Control Systems (FCS), a division of Fokker Space, said on Wednesday it won an order worth &quot;several million guilders&quot; to supply test apparatus to Indonesian aircraft maker IPTN.</p>
<p>Fokker Space, the 50 percent-owned engineering unit of bankrupt planemaker Fokker NV, said the apparatus would be used to test for metal fatigue in the N-250 passenger aircraft developed in Indonesia.</p>
<p>Fokker said the order, won against fierce competition, marked a breakthrough for FCS in the Far Eastern market.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
